    signature and its closing brace, for the eager struct and for its view.

    Included by `forge/rust/codec.rs.jinja2` twice. `view_decode` is false for
    the eager struct (`{Codec}<'a>`) and true for the view (`{Codec}View`, ADR
    0049), and picks what differs: the statement a list, an embedded body
    renders (`view_*` where the view holds it differently), the variant enum an
    arm is read into, the type an arm's body is, and how the value is made. The
    eager form of a codec that builds lists in place fills `_out` where its
    fields live; a view is a value of a few words and is built once, as a
    struct literal of what its reads return (docs/adr/0128). Every other field
    is read by the same statement on both. One skeleton, so a branch added here
    reaches both.

    `cursor` is the frame's reader (`SceReader`, docs/adr/0128): every read is
    total and records a refusal in it, so no statement here returns early and
    the frame's verdict is said once, by the caller that made the reader.

    `site_suffix` names the form each body this one holds is read by: the
    entry point, or the form held in place where this body is read on the
    build's hot path (docs/adr/0140). -#}
